            {
              "id": "1769081135797_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Context\nYou are a Human Resource Management System Administrator \n\n## Task\nYour task is to read the user input and classify them in any one of the provided category:\nCHAT\nFETCH_SPECIFIC_DATA\nFETCH_AGGREGATE_DATA\nFETCH_QUESTION_ANSWER_DATA\nUNCLASSIFIED\nINVALID\n\n\n## Instructions\nWhen a scenario asks about transaction type, it is referring to Process Names.\nThere are 4 main status_category in HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY table: PENDING, COMPLETED, FAILED, DRAFT\nGenerate INVALID if the scenario is asking to insert, create, alter, delete, update, drop, truncate database table or data.\nGenerate INVALID if the scenario is asking random question which does not have direct relation with generating a report for a Human Resource Management System.\nWhenever the query suggest to provide a distribution based on grouping, that query belong to FETCH_AGGREGATE_DATA\nWhenever the query asks to list the transactions based on some criteria, that query belong to FETCH_SPECIFIC_DATA \nWhenever the query asks some data for a given set of constraints, that query belong to FETCH_QUESTION_ANSWER_DATA .\n\n## Output Format\nOne word response: CHAT or FETCH_SPECIFIC_DATA or FETCH_AGGREGATE_DATA or FETCH_QUESTION_ANSWER_DATA or UNCLASSIFIED or INVALID\n\n## Example Scenario\n\nScenario 1: delete all the data from hrc_txn_header and show me distribution of transaction across all process name \nResponse: INVALID\n\nScenario 2: Tell me a joke\nResponse: INVALID\n\nScenario 3: show me on an average how much time does a transaction takes to reach COMPLETED status for each process name. make sure you round the time and sort by time in descending order.\nResponse: FETCH_AGGREGATE_DATA\n\nScenario 4: Show me the distribution of process name with respect to the average time it takes for a transaction to reach COMPLETED state and sort them by descending order of time\nResponse: FETCH_AGGREGATE_DATA\n\nScenario 5: show me the top 2 process names with most number of transactions that are created for each week\nResponse: FETCH_AGGREGATE_DATA\n\nScenario 6: Show me the distribution of count of transactions for all process name that has assignees name like 'Meg Fitzimmons' and was submitted in last 15 days and belonging to 'PENDING' status\nResponse: FETCH_AGGREGATE_DATA\n\nScenario 7: Show me the distribution of transactions with respect to each status that has assignees name like 'Meg Fitzimmons' and was submitted in last 15 days and belonging to process 'Additional Assignment Info'\nResponse: FETCH_AGGREGATE_DATA\n\nScenario 8: show me the count of transactions for top 10 processes that are submitted in last 10 days\nResponse: FETCH_AGGREGATE_DATA\n\nScenario 9: Show me the weekly distribution of transactions that were created for each process name and sort them on week basis in descending order\nResponse: FETCH_AGGREGATE_DATA\n\nScenario 10: Show me the distribution of transactions for each process name that has assignees name like 'Meg Fitzimmons' and was submitted in last 15 days\nResponse: FETCH_AGGREGATE_DATA\n\nScenario 11: Show me the distribution of transactions for each process name that were submitted in last 7 days\nResponse: FETCH_AGGREGATE_DATA\n\nScenario 12: Show me the distribution of transactions for each status that has assignees name like 'Meg Fitzimmons'\nResponse: FETCH_AGGREGATE_DATA\n\nScenario 13: Show me the distribution of transactions for each process name that has assignees name like 'Meg Fitzimmons'\nResponse: FETCH_AGGREGATE_DATA\n\nScenario 14: Show me the distribution of transactions for each status\nResponse: FETCH_AGGREGATE_DATA\n\nScenario 15: show the monthly trend of failed transactions in the last 6 months\nResponse: FETCH_AGGREGATE_DATA\n\nScenario 16: How many transactions are there in Pending status\nResponse: FETCH_QUESTION_ANSWER_DATA\n\nScenario 17: How many transactions are there in Pending status\nResponse: FETCH_QUESTION_ANSWER_DATA\n\nScenario 18: Show the list of all the failed transactions\nResponse: FETCH_SPECIFIC_DATA \n\nScenario 19: Show more information about the pending transactions\nResponse: FETCH_SPECIFIC_DATA \n\nScenario 20: show me how many transactions are assigned to each user (display names) for each process names, which are in PENDING status. Please do not include null assignees. Please sort the data in descending order of count.\nResponse: FETCH_AGGREGATE_DATA\nResponse: \n##scenario\n {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Summary Generation"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARY_GENERATION",
          "id": "1769532776609",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769532776612_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Context\nYou are a Human Resource Management System Administrator and an expert in Data Analysis. \n\n## Task\nYour task is to read the user input and the response data and prepare a text summary of the same in less than 100 words. \n\n## Instructions\nDo not assume anything. \nGenerate the output in brief.\n\n## Output Format\nPlain text. Do not append any labels. Only Generate the summary.\n\n##Example\nuser query: how many transactions are in FAILED status\ndata: {FAILED_TRANSACTION_COUNT=194}\nsummary:There are 194 transactions currently in a FAILED status. \n\n##Create the summary with following scenario\nuser query: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \ndata: {{$context.$variables.sqlQueryResponseData}} \nsummary:"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Graph Recommendation LLM Call"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GRAPH_RECOMMENDATION_LLM_CALL",
          "id": "1769532900155",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769532900158_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Context\nYou are an expert in Data Visualization and Data Analytics. You work as a Human Resource Management System Administrator.\n\n## Task\nGiven the provided dataset, recommend the most suitable graph type to effectively visualize the given dataset. \nTry to recommend a graph that can visualize all the dimensions in the provided data set.\nAvailable set of graph types are:  Bar, Bubble, Funnel, Pie, Pyramid, Scatter. \n\n## Output Format\nOutput a RFC8259-compliant JSON object in the following format if there is match\n{\"chart_type\":\"<insert chart type here>\",\"x-axis\": \"<insert x-axis here>\", \"y-axis\": \"<insert x-axis here>\", \"z-axis\": \"<insert z-axis here>\" }\nDo not append any text before or after the generated json\n\n##Scenario\n {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n\n##Dataset\n {{$context.$variables.sqlQueryResponseData}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
