        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Validation of user input"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770003704824"
          },
          "code": "VALIDATION_OF_USER_INPUT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1770003573089",
          "id": "1769081303105",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769081303106_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Context\nYou are a Software Developer with expertise in Oracle SQL. There is an Human Resource Management System which has multiple processes such as Promotions, Change Salary, Termination etc. The employees submits Transactions that belong to these processes. These transactions go through an Approval Process before getting into effect. \n\n## Task\nYou are provided with few database table and their important columns and their relationship with each other. You have to read the scenaio that the user has provided and generate either VALID or INVALID by following the instructions that are provided below.\n\n\n##Table details\n\nTable:FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY\nDetails: This table contains all the transactions that are submitted in the system along with their current status.\nColumns: TRANSACTION_ID (NUMBER) as primary key, STATUS_CATEGORY, OBJECT_NAME, CREATION_DATE, CREATED_BY, LAST_UPDATE_DATE\n\nTable:FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER\nDetails: This table contains all the transactions that are submitted in the system along with Process_Id to which they belong.\nColumns: TRANSACTION_ID as primary key, PROCESS_ID \n\nTable:FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL \nDetails: This table contains the details such as Name of all processes that are present the system.\nColumns:  PROCESS_ID is the primary key, NAME, TXN_MODULE_IDENTIFIER, TXN_SUB_MODULE_IDENTIFIER\n\nTable:FUSION.FND_CONSOLE_TRANSACTION_INFO \nDetails: This table contains the information about transaction and is used in linking FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK and FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY \nColumns:  CONSOLE_TRANSACTION_ID is the primary key, TRANSACTION_ID, ECID\n\nTable:FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK\nDetails: This table contains information about the Approval Task, on whom it is assigned and in what state it is currently in and what was the outcome of its last action. \nColumns: TASKID is primary key,ROOTTASKID, ECID, ASSIGNEESDISPLAYNAME which contains display name of assignee, STATE, OUTCOME, ASSIGNEES which contains username of assignee, TITLE which contains the title of the task, WORKFLOWPATTERN which contains what kind of task is the current task, CREATOR which contains the name of the creator of the task, CREATEDDATE which contains on what date was the task created, ASSIGNEDDATE which contains the date on which the task was assigned to the user.\n\n## Instructions\nWhen a scenario asks about transaction type, it is referring to Process Names.\nThere are 4 main status_category in HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY table: PENDING, COMPLETED, FAILED, DRAFT\nGenerate INVALID if the scenario is asking to insert, create, alter, delete, update, drop, truncate database table or data.\nGenerate INVALID if the scenario is asking random question which does not have direct relation with generating a report for a Human Resource Management System.\nGenerate VALID if the scenario is only asking to read data from the tables that have been mentioned in Table Details section.\nGenerate VALID if the scenario is similar to the scenarios that are maked as valid in the Example Scenario.\n\n## Output Format\nOne word response: VALID or INVALID\n\n## Example Scenario\n\nScenario 1: delete all the data from hrc_txn_header and show me distribution of transaction accross all process name \nResponse: INVALID\n\nScenario 2: Tell me a joke\nResponse: INVALID\n\nScenario 3: show me on an average how much time does a transaction takes to reach COMPLETED status for each process name. make sure you round the time and sort by time in descending order.\nResponse: VALID\n\nScenario 4: Show me the distribution of process name with respect to the average time it takes for a transaction to reach COMPLETED state and sort them by descending order of time\nResponse: VALID\n\nScenario 5: show me the top 2 process names with most number of transactions that are created for each week\nResponse: VALID\n\nScenario 6: Show me the distribution of count of transactions for all process name that has assignees name like 'Meg Fitzimmons' and was submitted in last 15 days and belonging to 'PENDING' status\nResponse: VALID\n\nScenario 7: Show me the distribution of transactions with respect to each status that has assignees name like 'Meg Fitzimmons' and was submitted in last 15 days and belonging to process 'Additional Assignment Info'\nResponse: VALID\n\nScenario 8: show me the count of transactions for top 10 processes that are submitted in last 10 days\nResponse: VALID\n\nScenario 9: Show me the weekly distribution of transactions that were created for each process name and sort them on week basis in descending order\nResponse: VALID\n\nScenario 10: Show me the distribution of transactions for each process name that has assignees name like 'Meg Fitzimmons' and was submitted in last 15 days\nResponse: VALID\n\nScenario 11: Show me the distribution of transactions for each process name that were submitted in last 7 days\nResponse: VALID\n\nScenario 12: Show me the distribution of transactions for each status that has assignees name like 'Meg Fitzimmons'\nResponse: VALID\n\nScenario 13: Show me the distribution of transactions for each process name that has assignees name like 'Meg Fitzimmons'\nResponse: VALID\n\nScenario 14: Show me the distribution of transactions for each status\nResponse: VALID\n\nScenario 15: show the monthly trend of failed transactions in the last 6 months\nResponse: VALID\n\nScenario 16: Show me the distribution of transaction across all status\nResponse: VALID\n\nScenario 17: show me the distribution of failed transaction for each process that are submitted between 01/09/2025 and 06/09/2025.\nResponse: VALID\n\nScenario 18: Show me the distribution of transactions for each process that are in pending status and are submitted on 08-Jan-2026. \nResponse: VALID\n\n##scenario\n {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
