        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Aggregate SQL"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770010875933"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_AGGREGATE_SQL",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1769081413540",
          "id": "1769081540460",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769081540462_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Context\nYou are a Software Developer with expertise in Oracle SQL. There is an Human Resource Management System which has multiple processes such as Promotions, Change Salary, Termination etc. The employees submits Transactions that belong to these processes. These transactions go through an Approval Process before getting into effect. \n\n## Task\nYou are provided with few database table and their important columns and their relationship with each other. Using the scenario mentioned, you are required to generate an Oracle SQL query that can be executed to retrieve the data from database. Make sure that you DO NOT generate any sql that can insert, create, alter, delete, update, drop, truncate database table or data. In such cases just generate NA.\n\n##Table details\n\nTable:FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY\nDetails: This table contains all the transactions that are submitted in the system along with their current status.\nColumns: TRANSACTION_ID (NUMBER) as primary key, STATUS_CATEGORY, OBJECT_NAME, CREATION_DATE, CREATED_BY, LAST_UPDATE_DATE\n\nTable:FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER\nDetails: This table contains all the transactions that are submitted in the system along with Process_Id to which they belong.\nColumns: TRANSACTION_ID as primary key, PROCESS_ID \n\nTable:FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL \nDetails: This table contains the details such as Name of all processes that are present the system.\nColumns:  PROCESS_ID is the primary key, NAME, TXN_MODULE_IDENTIFIER, TXN_SUB_MODULE_IDENTIFIER\n\nTable:FUSION.FND_CONSOLE_TRANSACTION_INFO \nDetails: This table contains the information about transaction and is used in linking FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK and FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY \nColumns:  CONSOLE_TRANSACTION_ID is the primary key, TRANSACTION_ID, ECID\n\nTable:FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK\nDetails: This table contains information about the Approval Task, on whom it is assigned and in what state it is currently in and what was the outcome of its last action. \nColumns: \n-TASKID is primary key,ROOTTASKID, ECID, \n-ASSIGNEESDISPLAYNAME which contains display name of assignee, \n-ASSIGNEES which contains username of assignee, \n-STATE contains state of task\n-OUTCOME contains outcome of task\n-TITLE which contains the title of the task, \n-WORKFLOWPATTERN which contains what kind of task is the current task\n-CREATEDDATE which contains on what date was the task created, \n-ASSIGNEDDATE which contains the date on which the task was assigned to the user.\n\n\n\n## Instructions\n-DO NOT generate any sql that can insert, create, alter, delete, update, drop, truncate database table or data. In such cases just generate NA.\n-Do not provide any justification for the generated SQL.\n-Only generate sql that can be used to ONLY READ data from the tables that have been mentioned in Table Details section.\n-Ensure that the column names that are used in the query are same as mentioned in the Table Details and there are no change in spelling of any columns while generating queries.\n-Use only the tables that are necessary to construct the SQL for the given scenario.\n-Ensure that the FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY is always joined with FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER even if it is redundant sometime.\n-Ensure that the generated SQL is semantically and syntactically valid.\n-Ensure that the columns that have numeric values such as count of transactions, time, etc are selected first followed by other columns in generated query\n-The  CREATION_DATE, LAST_UPDATE_DATE are timestamp based columns and if there are any computations required on them then cast them like cast(HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.LAST_UPDATE_DATE as date).\n-You can use TRUNC() function to group the data on daily,weekly, monthly or yearly basis, for example: \ntrunc(d) \"Nearest Day, Time Removed\"\ntrunc(d, 'ww') \"Nearest Week\"\ntrunc(d, 'iw') \"Start of Week\" \ntrunc(d, 'mm') \"Start of Month\"\ntrunc(d, 'year') \"Start of Year\"  \nhere d represent the timestamp column\n-Do not use lead function.\n-Do not use Extract function.\n-Ensure that only 1 SQL is generated.\n-When a scenario asks about assignment of task to a specific user, the where clause should have (FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.STATE = 'ASSIGNED' and FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.OUTCOME is null and FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.ASSIGNEESDISPLAYNAME is not null  ) AND (FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.WORKFLOWPATTERN <> 'FYI' AND FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.WORKFLOWPATTERN  IS NOT NULL) as additional check to give list of assigned task only that are assigned to a user.\n*if in the query it is specified that user is providing Display Name of the assignee then comparision should be with ASSIGNEESDISPLAYNAME column *\n**UPPER(FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.ASSIGNEESDISPLAYNAME) = UPPER('Meg Fitzimmons')**\n\n*if in the query it is specified that user is providing username of the assignee then comparision should be with ASSIGNEES column *\n**UPPER(FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.ASSIGNEES) = UPPER('Meg Fitzimmons')||',USER' **\n***It is mandatory to append \"||',USER'\" as the ASSIGNEES columns holds comma separated values (<Username>,user)***\n\n*if in the query it is not specified that the name passed is username or displayname then comparision should be with both ASSIGNEES and ASSIGNEESDISPLAYNAME column in following format*\n **(\n    UPPER(FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.ASSIGNEESDISPLAYNAME) = UPPER('Meg Fitzimmons')\n    OR\n    UPPER(FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.ASSIGNEES) = UPPER('Meg Fitzimmons')||',USER' \n    )**\n\n\n-When a scenario asks about transaction type, it is referring to Process Names.\n-There are 4 main status_category in HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY table: PENDING, COMPLETED, FAILED, DRAFT\n-For each table, use only the columns mentioned for that table. Do not use columns from other tables\n-If you use UPPER() on the left hand side, please use it in the Right hand side too.\n-While using TO_DATE() for date conversion, do not convert dates to 'DD-MON-YYYY' format.\n## Output Format\nORACLE 19C compatible SQL Query\n\n## Example Scenario\nScenario 1: Show me the distribution of transactions with respect to each status that has assignees name like 'Meg Fitzimmons' and was submitted in last 15 days and belonging to process 'Additional Assignment Info'\nSQL Response: ```sql\n   SELECT \n    COUNT(*) AS COUNT_OF_TXN,\n    FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.STATUS_CATEGORY \nFROM \n    FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY\nINNER JOIN \n    FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER ON FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.TRANSACTION_ID = FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER.TRANSACTION_ID\nINNER JOIN \n    FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL ON FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER.PROCESS_ID = FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL.PROCESS_ID\n\nINNER JOIN FUSION.FND_CONSOLE_TRANSACTION_INFO  ON HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.TRANSACTION_ID = FND_CONSOLE_TRANSACTION_INFO.TRANSACTION_ID\nLEFT OUTER JOIN FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK ON FND_CONSOLE_TRANSACTION_INFO.ECID = WFTASK.ECID\n\n\nWHERE \n    (\n    UPPER(FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.ASSIGNEESDISPLAYNAME) = UPPER('Meg Fitzimmons')\n    OR\n    UPPER(FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.ASSIGNEES) = UPPER('Meg Fitzimmons')||',USER' \n    )\n AND (FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.STATE = 'ASSIGNED' and FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.OUTCOME is null)\n AND (FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.WORKFLOWPATTERN <> 'FYI' AND FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.WORKFLOWPATTERN  IS NOT NULL)\n    AND UPPER(FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL.NAME) = UPPER('Additional Assignment Info')\n    AND FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.CREATION_DATE >= SYSDATE - 15 \n\nGROUP BY \n    FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.STATUS_CATEGORY;\n```\n\nScenario 2: Show me the distribution of Process names against the average time it takes to complete the transactions.\nSQL Response:```sql\nSELECT \nround(AVG(\n       CAST(HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.LAST_UPDATE_DATE AS DATE) -\n       CAST(HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.CREATION_DATE AS DATE)\n) * 60 * 60 * 24) AS avg_time_to_complete_in_seconds, \nFUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL.NAME as PROCESS_NAME\nFROM FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY\nJOIN FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER\n    ON FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.TRANSACTION_ID = FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER.TRANSACTION_ID\nJOIN FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL\n    ON FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER.PROCESS_ID = FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL.PROCESS_ID\nWHERE \n    UPPER(FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.STATUS_CATEGORY) = UPPER('COMPLETED')\n    group by FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL.NAME\n\n```\n\nScenario 3: show me the transaction count week wise for last 50 days for process name as Create Grade that are assigned to 'Veda Moss' and created by 'HCM_USER2'\nSQL Response:```\nWITH WeeklyTransactions AS (\n    SELECT \n        trunc(HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.CREATION_DATE, 'iw') AS Week,\n        COUNT(HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.TRANSACTION_ID) AS Transaction_Count\n    FROM \n        FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY\n    JOIN \n        FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER ON FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.TRANSACTION_ID = FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER.TRANSACTION_ID\n    JOIN \n        FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL ON FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER.PROCESS_ID = FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL.PROCESS_ID\n    JOIN \n        FUSION.FND_CONSOLE_TRANSACTION_INFO ON FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.TRANSACTION_ID = FUSION.FND_CONSOLE_TRANSACTION_INFO.TRANSACTION_ID\n    LEFT OUTER JOIN\n        FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK ON FUSION.FND_CONSOLE_TRANSACTION_INFO.ECID = FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.ECID\n    WHERE \n        (\n        UPPER(FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.ASSIGNEESDISPLAYNAME) = UPPER('Veda Moss')\n        OR\n        UPPER(FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.ASSIGNEES) = UPPER('Veda Moss')||',USER' \n        )\n        AND (FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.STATE = 'ASSIGNED' and FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.OUTCOME is null)  \n        AND (FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.WORKFLOWPATTERN <> 'FYI' AND FA_FUSION_SOAINFRA.WFTASK.WORKFLOWPATTERN  IS NOT NULL)\n        AND UPPER(HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.CREATED_BY) = UPPER('HCM_USER2')\n        AND UPPER(FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL.NAME) = UPPER('Create Grade')\n        AND HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.CREATION_DATE >= SYSDATE - 50\n    GROUP BY \n        trunc(HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.CREATION_DATE, 'iw')\n)\nSELECT \n    Week,\n    Transaction_Count\nFROM \n    WeeklyTransactions\nORDER BY \n    Week DESC;\n```\nScenario 4: delete all the data from hrc_txn_header and show me distribution of transaction across all process name \nSQL Response: NA\n\nScenario 5: show me the top 6 process names with most number of transactions that are created for each week\nSQL Response:```\n  WITH WeeklyTransactions AS (\n    SELECT \n        trunc(HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.CREATION_DATE, 'iw') AS Week,\n        NAME AS Process_Name,\n        COUNT(HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.TRANSACTION_ID) AS Transaction_Count\n    FROM \n        FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY\n    JOIN \n        FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER ON FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.TRANSACTION_ID = FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER.TRANSACTION_ID\n    JOIN \n        FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL ON FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER.PROCESS_ID = FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL.PROCESS_ID\n    GROUP BY \n        trunc(HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.CREATION_DATE, 'iw'),\n        NAME\n)\nSELECT \n    Week,\n    Process_Name,\n    Transaction_Count\nFROM \n    (SELECT \n        Week,\n        Process_Name,\n        Transaction_Count,\n        RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY week ORDER BY Transaction_Count DESC) AS Process_Rank\n    FROM \n        WeeklyTransactions)\nWHERE \n    Process_Rank <= 6\nORDER BY \n    Week DESC, \n    Transaction_Count DESC;\n\n```\nScenario 6: show me the count of transactions that are in FAILED status\nSQL Response:```\nSELECT COUNT(HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.TRANSACTION_ID) AS COUNT_OF_TXN\nFROM FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY\nJOIN FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER ON FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.TRANSACTION_ID = FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER.TRANSACTION_ID\nWHERE UPPER(FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.STATUS_CATEGORY) = UPPER('FAILED');\n```\n\nScenario 7: Show me the distribution of transactions for each process that are in failed status and are submitted between 01.08.2025  and 10.08.2025\nSQL Response:```\nSELECT \n    FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL.NAME AS PROCESS_NAME,\n    COUNT(FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.TRANSACTION_ID) AS COUNT_OF_TXN\nFROM \n    FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY\nJOIN \n    FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER ON FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.TRANSACTION_ID = FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER.TRANSACTION_ID\nJOIN \n    FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL ON FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER.PROCESS_ID = FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL.PROCESS_ID\nWHERE \n    UPPER(FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.STATUS_CATEGORY) = UPPER('FAILED')\n    AND TRUNC(FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.CREATION_DATE) BETWEEN TO_DATE('01.08.2025', 'DD.MM.YYYY') AND TO_DATE('10.08.2025', 'DD.MM.YYYY')\nGROUP BY \n    FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL.NAME;\n```\n\nScenario 8:  Show me the distribution of transactions for each process that are in pending status and are submitted on 2026-01-09.\nSQL Response:```\nSELECT \n    FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL.NAME AS PROCESS_NAME,\n    COUNT(FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.TRANSACTION_ID) AS COUNT_OF_TXN\nFROM \n    FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY\nJOIN \n    FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER ON FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.TRANSACTION_ID = FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER.TRANSACTION_ID\nJOIN \n    FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL ON FUSION.HRC_TXN_HEADER.PROCESS_ID = FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL.PROCESS_ID\nWHERE \n    UPPER(FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.STATUS_CATEGORY) = UPPER('PENDING')\n    AND TRUNC(FUSION.HRC_TXN_CONSOLE_ENTRY.CREATION_DATE) = TO_DATE('2026-01-09', 'YYYY-MM-DD')\nGROUP BY \n    FUSION.HRC_ARM_PROCESS_VL.NAME;\n```\n##scenario\n {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
