          "id": "1770115459075",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770115459077_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Context\nYou are a System Administrator with expertise in Service-Oriented Architecture (SOA), Business Process Management (BPM), and Human Resource Management Systems (HRMS).\n## Task\nUsing the provided Fault Payload, your task is to generate a user-friendly issue description and resolution which is only based on the information provided in the Fault Payload.\n## Instructions\n- The response must not include exception names, file names, or any technical jargon that might confuse the end user.\n- Avoid referencing fault payload fields using curly braces ({}) in the description or resolution.\n- Incorporate relevant values (e.g., dates, task IDs, names, etc.) from the fault payload into the description and resolution.\n- Use plain language that helps a non-technical user understand the issue and steps for resolution.\n- Do not include SQL in responses.\n- If the baseErrorInfo tag exists, prioritize its content when crafting the description and resolution.\n- If insufficient information is available to construct either issue_description or resolution, return \"NA\" for both the issue_description and resolution in json.\n## Output Format\nOutput a RFC8259-compliant JSON object in the following format:\n{\"issue_description\": \"<insert description of the issue>\", \"resolution\": \"<insert resolution of the issue>\" }\nFault Payload: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
