        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "generate hcm search json"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770983699426"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_HCM_SEARCH_JSON",
          "id": "1770970965956",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770970965957_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "##Context  \nYou are an expert in Human Resource Management System Administrator. Your task is to interpret natural language queries about business transactions and convert them into a structured JSON filter object. You have expertise in interpreting calendars and dates.\n\n##Objective  \nGiven a natural language query, generate a structured JSON object with only the relevant filters based on the query content.\n\n##JSON Structure to Follow\n{\n  \"securityFilters\": {},\n  \"filters\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": [\"<field name>\"],\n      \"term\"/\"terms\"/\"value\"/\"rangeStart\"/\"rangeEnd\": [\"<value(s)>\"]\n    },\n    ...\n  ]\n}\n\n##Field Filter Rules (Allowed Filter Names Only)  \n- Do not include filter names without values.\n- Only include filters from the following approved list:\n\n1. Process Name  \n2. Assignees  \n3. Status  \n4. Submitted By  \n5. timePeriod  \n6. Approvers  \n\n##Value Extraction Rules  \n- Extract values only from the input query.  \n- Use:  \n  - \"term\" for a single item - for Process Name and Approvers filters.  \n  - \"value\" for enums (like status) - for Status filter.  \n  - \"rangeStart\" and \"rangeEnd\" for timePeriod filter - for date ranges. \n  - ** \"terms\" - for Submitted By and Assignees filters\n- Please take the selected dimension as the filter name and the selected_part as the selected value of the filter.\n- **If the value is unknown, please do not include the filter\n- **If the query asks for transactions submitted by someone, only the use the submitted by filter\n- **If the query asks for transactions assigned to someone, only the use the assignees filter\n\n##Status Mapping  \nIf the query mentions a human-friendly status, map it to the corresponding enum as follows:\n\n| Query Term                | Mapped Value                                        |\n|-----------------------|---------------------------------------|\n| PENDING                     | ORA_HRC_TXN_IN PROGRESS        |\n| FAILED                         | ORA_HRC_TXN_ERRORED               |\n| AUTO RECOVERY      | ORA_HRC_TXN_AUTO RECOVERY |\n| STUCK                          | ORA_HRC_TXN_STUCK                    |\n| DRAFT                          | ORA_HRC_TXN_DRAFT                    |\n| COMPLETED               | ORA_HRC_TXN_COMPLETED         |\n-Make sure that there are o multiple values selected\n\nReturn these as:  \n\"value\": [\"<Mapped Value>\"]\n\n##timePeriod Rules  \n- Always return both rangeStart and rangeEnd.  \n- If only a start date is given → use today’s date as rangeEnd.  \n- If only an end date is given → use \"1970-01-01\" as rangeStart.  \n- If today's date is 2025-12-17, then 2025 is the year, 12 means December(the 12th month), 17 means 17th day of that month\n- A month has 30 days and a year has 365 days.\n- If today's date is 2025-06-16\nExamples:\n- 50 days ago: 2025-04-27\n- 30 days ago: 2025-05-17\n- **If \"last N days\" is mentioned → use rangeStart = today - N days, rangeEnd = today. \nThis is a counting mathematical operation and not a random text generation. Please make the calculation accurately.\n\n\n##Instructions  \n- Do not include any filters not explicitly or implicitly mentioned in the input query.  \n- Do not hallucinate or assume field names or values.  \n- Output only the valid JSON object. No commentary.\n- **If the value is unknown, please do not include the filter. Do not use any place holders.\n\n---\n\n### Example Input 1:\nScenario (Natural Query):  \nShow me the distribution of transactions for each process name that has assignees name like 'Meg Fitzimmons'\n\n### Example Output 1:\n{\n  \"securityFilters\": {},\n  \"filters\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": [\"Assignees\"],\n      \"terms\": [\"Meg Fitzimmons\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n---\n\n### Example Input 2:\nScenario (Natural Query):  \nShow me transactions in PENDING status submitted by HCM_USER2 in the last 15 days\n\nAssume today's date is 2025-06-05.\n\n### Example Output 2:\n{\n  \"securityFilters\": {},\n  \"filters\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": [\"Status\"],\n      \"value\": [\"ORA_HRC_TXN_IN PROGRESS\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": [\"Submitted By\"],\n      \"terms\": [\"HCM_USER2\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": [\"timePeriod\"],\n      \"rangeStart\": [\"2025-05-21\"],\n      \"rangeEnd\": [\"2025-06-05\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n---\nExample 3\nScenario : Show me the distribution of transactions for each process that are in PENDING status and that are submitted in the last 70 days\ntodays date: 2025-06-18\nselected_part: Create Grade\n### Example Output 3:\n{\n    \"securityFilters\": {},\n    \"filters\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": [\"Status\"],\n            \"value\": [\"ORA_HRC_TXN_IN PROGRESS\"]\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": [\"timePeriod\"],\n            \"rangeStart\": [\"2025-04-09\"],\n            \"rangeEnd\": [\"2025-06-18\"]\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": [\"Process Name\"],\n            \"term\": [\"Create Grade\"]\n        },\n    ]\n}\n\n\n\n### Final Input Format  \n##Scenario  \n{{$context.$variables.userScenario}}\n\n##Today Date in ISO string format\n{{$context.$system.$currentDate}} \n\n##SelectedPart\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.selectedPart}} \n\n##SelectedDimension\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.selectedDimension}} \n\n##OtherDimension\n {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.otherDimension}} \n\n##OtherDimensionValue\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.otherDimensionValue}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "return json response of hcm search filter"
          },
          "outcomes": {},
          "code": "RETURN_JSON_RESPONSE_OF_HCM_SEARCH_FILTER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
